          "id": "12381858",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "Just a simple question:\nHow would the server know which encoding was used for the multipart headers?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2004-08-02T14:00:07.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-08-02T14:00:07.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333927/comment/12381859",
          "id": "12381859",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=adrian%40ephox.com",
            "name": "adrian@ephox.com",
            "key": "adrian@ephox.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Adrian Sutton",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "According to RFC 2388 (http://www.faqs.org/rfcs/rfc2388.html), section 3, the encoding of header \nvalues is ASCII but non-ASCII characters may be encoded according to RFC2047 (http://www.faqs.org/\nrfcs/rfc2047.html) which is MIME encoding.  So as far as I can tell this patch is incorrect but we may \nwant to consider having the capability for HttpClient to use RFC2047 encoding automatically when \nrequired.\n\nThe current workaround is to simply specify the header values pre-encoded according to RFC2047.\n\nDoes that seem right to anyone else?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=adrian%40ephox.com",
            "name": "adrian@ephox.com",
            "key": "adrian@ephox.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Adrian Sutton",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2004-08-02T14:52:37.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-08-02T14:52:37.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333927/comment/12381860",
          "id": "12381860",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "Adrian,\n\nThanks for the hint to RFC-2388. However I am unsure if it really applies here,\nas RFC-2388 covers \"multipart/form-data\" only.",
